WEBVTT

00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.431
This man's title is on lunch menus

00:00:02.441 --> 00:00:03.646
all over the world.

00:00:03.656 --> 00:00:06.685
John Montagu, the fourth Earl of Sandwich,

00:00:06.695 --> 00:00:09.258
painted by Gainsborough in 1783.

00:00:09.358 --> 00:00:10.669
The famous story:

00:00:10.679 --> 00:00:13.169
he gambled for twenty-four
hours, living on

00:00:13.179 --> 00:00:15.192
beef between slices of toast.

00:00:15.202 --> 00:00:18.728
That comes from one French
traveller, Pierre-Jean

00:00:18.738 --> 00:00:21.388
Grosley, who visited London in 1765.

00:00:21.488 --> 00:00:23.513
And he never even names the earl.

00:00:23.523 --> 00:00:24.846
The word is older.

00:00:24.856 --> 00:00:27.987
In 1762, the historian Edward Gibbon saw

00:00:27.997 --> 00:00:30.652
top Londoners at a club, supping on

00:00:30.662 --> 00:00:32.621
cold meat, "or a Sandwich".

00:00:32.745 --> 00:00:34.310
So the earl didn't invent bread with

00:00:34.320 --> 00:00:35.610
something inside.

00:00:35.620 --> 00:00:36.885
He gave it a name, and the

00:00:36.895 --> 00:00:37.956
name stuck.

00:00:37.966 --> 00:00:40.002
Every time you order one, you're saying

00:00:40.012 --> 00:00:41.325
this man's title.
